    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d183">

                <pb facs="0332" n="1298" sameAs="frus:frus1951v04p2/pg1298"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">No. 648</seg>
                </opener>
                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.5/10–3051: Telegram</note>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States Deputy Representative on the North
                        Atlantic Council (Spofford) to the Acting Secretary of
                            State
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d183-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-10-30T13:00:00+00:00">October 30, 1951—1
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    Depto 528. Deps 75th mtg Oct 29.</p>
                <p>3. Some deps without instructions<anchor n="2" xml:id="d183-f2"/> but most agreed
                    with US, UK, Fr and Neth that origins of Moscow econ conf in World Peace Council
                    and Sov failure to use existing econ orgs indicate it is purely propaganda move,
                    aimed at securing non-Commie signatures to anodyne resolution, emphasizing
                    “peaceful coexistence” and E-W trade, and UK suggested, possibly aimed at
                    creation of org to rival OEEC. Deps will
                    discuss further but generally agreed best policy is to discourage attendance and
                    expose nature of conf.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d183-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Spofford</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d183-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d183-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to the other NATO capitals, Frankfurt,
                    Heidelberg, and Wiesbaden.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d183-f2" n="2" xml:id="d183-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram Depto 506 from London, October 25,
                    reported that the North Atlantic Council Deputies, at their 73d meeting on
                    October 24, reacted generally favorably to the U.S. suggestion that the Moscow
                    Economic Conference be the subject of an early discussion after the Deputies had
                    obtained the views of their governments. (740.5/10–2551)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d183-f3" n="3" xml:id="d183-f3-content">
                <p>A paraphrase of this paragraph was transmitted in a circular information telegram
                    of October 31. (700.00(S)/10–3151)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
